Description: Directory Opus
Author: Andrew Rathbun, Dielle De Noon
Version: 1.2
Id: 31a9022d-bd2e-4031-97c1-046b51bfcc7d
RecreateDirectories: true
Targets:
    -
        Name: Directory Opus MRU
        Category: Apps
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\AppData\Local\GPSoftware\Directory Opus\State Data\MRU\
        Recursive: true
        Comment: "All MRU state files (rename, find, dupe, sync, browse, select actions) - filenames vary by version, hence recursive rather than a fixed list."
    -
        Name: Directory Opus State Data
        Category: Apps
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\AppData\Local\GPSoftware\Directory Opus\State Data\
        FileMask: '*'
        Comment: "State Data root files (archives, network cache, prefs, theme, window state, etc.) excluding the MRU subfolder, covered above."
    -
        Name: Directory Opus Thumbnail Cache
        Category: Apps
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\AppData\Local\GPSoftware\Directory Opus\Thumbnail Cache\
        Comment: "Thumbnail cache - randomized filenames with a .db extension."
    -
        Name: Directory Opus Logs
        Category: Apps
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\AppData\Roaming\GPSoftware\Directory Opus\Logs\
        Comment: "Locates .txt files that will be named with the IP address of the FTP server Directory Opus was used to connect to."

# Documentation
# Directory Opus is a popular Windows File Explorer replacement.
# State Data\MRU and State Data root filenames vary between Directory Opus versions and which features
# the user has used (rename, find, duplicate finder, synchronize, select, etc.), so these two targets use
# Recursive/wildcard matching rather than an exact filename list. Any of the .osd files can be viewed in
# a text editor. The Thumbnail Cache folder contains randomized filenames with a .db extension.
